# Every tracked file in this project is a shell script, a config template or a
# test that runs on Linux (Alpine / iSH-AOK / Debian / Arch / ...).
#
# Git stores them with LF, but Windows installs commonly set
# core.autocrlf=true system-wide, which rewrites the working tree to CRLF on
# checkout. A shell script with CRLF line endings fails immediately on Linux:
#
#     ./install.sh: line 28: syntax error near unexpected token `$'{\r''
#
# Pinning eol=lf here keeps the working tree usable on every platform,
# regardless of the machine's autocrlf setting.

* text=auto eol=lf

*.sh    text eol=lf
*.conf  text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf

# Leave anything binary alone.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.gz    binary
*.zst   binary
*.xz    binary
